ient-seminorm-triangle-inequality","thm-quotient-seminorm-is-a-norm-iff-subspace-is-closed","thm-quotient-map-is-open","thm-quotient-of-banach-by-closed-subspace-is-banach","thm-universal-property-of-the-normed-quotient"]},{"convention":"The sequence-space examples and the counting-measure corollary index sequences from $n=0$.","fixed_by":"cor-ell-p-duality-by-counting-measure","matters_for":["ex-the-dual-of-ell-two-is-ell-two-by-the-counting-measure-pairing","ex-shift-operators-on-classical-sequence-spaces","cex-a-closed-subspace-need-not-have-a-best-approximation","cex-an-algebraic-complement-need-not-be-topological"]},{"convention":"The Chebyshev functions use real cutoffs, with $\\theta(x)=\\sum_{p\\le x}\\log p$ and $\\psi(x)=\\sum_{n\\le x}\\Lambda(n)$.","fixed_by":"def-chebyshev-psi-function","matters_for":["lem-chebyshev-psi-prime-power-expansion","lem-prime-counting-chebyshev-partial-summation","thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","lem-chebyshev-functions-prime-power-comparison","thm-chebyshev-prime-counting-bounds","ex-prime-counting-theta-and-psi-table"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-an-l-q-function-defines-a-bounded-linear-functional-on-l-p","statement":"For each $g\\in L^q(\\mu)$, $\\Lambda_g([f])=\\int fg\\,d\\mu$ defines a bounded linear functional on $L^p(\\mu)$ and $|\\Lambda_g([f])|\\le\\|[f]\\|_p\\|g\\|_q$.","used_by":["prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","prop-semifinite-measures-make-l-q-representatives-unique","lem-rn-densities-of-bounded-l-p-functionals-belong-to-l-q","thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p"]},{"id":"prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","statement":"For $g\\in L^q(\\mu)$, $\\|\\Lambda_g\\|=\\|g\\|_q$ when $1<p<\\infty$, and also when $p=1$ provided $\\mu$ is semifinite.","used_by":["prop-semifinite-measures-make-l-q-representatives-unique","lem-rn-densities-of-bounded-l-p-functionals-belong-to-l-q","thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p","thm-arbitrary-measure-duality-for-l-p-when-one-less-p-less-infinity","cor-l-p-norm-recovery-by-unit-l-q-pairings"]},{"id":"def-bounded-linear-operator","statement":"A linear $T:X\\to Y$ over one scalar field is bounded when $\\|Tx\\|\\le C\\|x\\|$ for all $x$ and some real $C\\ge0$.","used_by":["thm-bounded-linear-operator-equivalences","def-operator-norm","def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators","thm-bounded-operator-space-is-banach","thm-extension-of-a-bounded-map-from-a-dense-subspace","def-bounded-below-operator","def-bounded-left-and-right-inverses"]},{"id":"def-quotient-seminorm","statement":"For $M\\le X$, $\\|x+M\\|_{X/M}=\\inf_{m\\in M}\\|x+m\\|=\\operatorname{dist}(x,M)$.","used_by":["lem-quotient-seminorm-is-representative-independent","lem-quotient-seminorm-triangle-inequality","thm-quotient-seminorm-is-a-norm-iff-subspace-is-closed","thm-quotient-map-is-open","thm-quotient-of-banach-by-closed-subspace-is-banach","thm-universal-property-of-the-normed-quotient"]},{"id":"thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","statement":"There are $0<c<C$ and $x_0$ such that $cx\\le\\theta(x)\\le Cx$ for every real $x\\ge x_0$.","used_by":["lem-chebyshev-functions-prime-power-comparison","thm-chebyshev-prime-counting-bounds","lem-weighted-von-mangoldt-harmonic-estimate","cex-chebyshev-bounds-do-not-give-the-prime-number-theorem"]},{"id":"thm-second-mertens-theorem-for-primes","statement":"$\\sum_{p\\le x}1/p=\\log\\log x+B_1+O(1/\\log x)$.","used_by":["thm-third-mertens-theorem-for-primes","cor-sum-of-reciprocals-of-primes-diverges","cex-shoups-product-bound-does-not-determine-mertens-constant"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions","used_for":"The class-versus-representative convention in $L^p$ duality.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals","used_for":"Integrability and the pairing bound for $\\Lambda_g$.","opened":true},{"id":"prop-essential-supremum-is-attained-as-the-least-essential-bound","used_for":"The $L^\\infty$ endpoint 