 convergence to prove $\\|[w_n]-[f]\\|_p\\to0$, but the item has no dominated-convergence dependency or fact; [L3] is monotone convergence.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"lem-chebyshev-psi-prime-power-expansion","concern":"Step 3.1 applies [L3] to $\\theta(x^{1/k})$ for every $k\\ge1$, while [L3] is stated only for arguments at least $2$. The definition's empty-sum remark resolves the remaining case but is not supplied by [L3].","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","concern":"Step 1.2 derives the valuation-layer estimate $\\log\\binom{2n}{n}\\le\\theta(2n)+R_n$ from [L2], but [L2] as restated omits the valuation expansion needed for that derivation.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-extension-of-a-bounded-map-from-a-dense-subspace","concern":"In step 5.1 the strict bound $\\|Td_n(x)\\|<C(\\|x\\|+1/n)$ is invalid when the permitted bound is $C=0$. A separate zero-operator argument closes the case.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"lem-bounded-functionals-on-finite-l-p-define-finite-signed-or-complex-measures","concern":"[L1] attributes continuity to the bounded-functional definition, although that definition gives linearity and a norm inequality only. Step 3.1 needs continuity, which follows immediately from the bound but is not stated or derived.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}